.TH VAULT-CLIENT 1 "2026-08-19" "mu2edaq-notify 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
vault_client.py \- fetch mu2edaq-pager secrets from HashiCorp Vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 scripts/vault_client.py
.RI [ env | helm-values | json ]
[\fB\-\-env\fR \fIprod\fR|\fItest\fR]
[\fB\-\-addr\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-base\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-kv\-mount\fR \fIMOUNT\fR]
[\fB\-\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR]
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vault_client.py
reads mu2edaq-pager secrets from a HashiCorp Vault KV v2 engine and renders them
in one of three formats for a consumer:
.BR env " (KEY=\(dqvalue\(dq lines),"
.BR helm-values " (a YAML fragment matching " helm/values.yaml ","
used by
.BR deploy\-okd\-proxy.sh (1)),
or
.BR json .
.PP
.B SECRET_REGISTRY
at the top of the script currently carries one entry: the Kerberos
keytab and principal for the optional SSH-tunnel sidecar
.RB ( backend.tunnel.enabled " in " helm/values.yaml ).
An unpopulated section reads as empty rather than erroring, so this
stays a no-op for direct-mode deploys. See
.B docs/Vault-Secrets.md
for how to add the first one.
.PP
There are two separate secret instances, production and test, each with
its own base path
.RI ( okd/shared/prod/mu2edaq-pager " and " okd/shared/test/mu2edaq-pager ).
.B \-\-env
selects between them; if omitted, it defaults to
.I test
so nothing reads production secrets without an explicit choice.
.PP
It never implements Vault's login flow itself. Human developers
authenticate with the
.B vault
CLI
.RB ( "vault login \-method=ldap \-address=https://ssivault.fnal.gov:8200" ),
which caches a token at
.IR ~/.vault-token ;
this script only reads that cached token (or
.B \-\-token
/
.BR VAULT_TOKEN ).
.PP
Which secret lives at which Vault path, under which env var and Helm value
name, is defined once in the
.B SECRET_REGISTRY
list at the top of the script \(en see
.B docs/Vault-Secrets.md
for the full table.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I env|helm-values|json
Output format. Required, positional.
.TP
.BI \-\-env " prod|test"
Which secret instance to read.
.br
Precedence: this flag >
.B VAULT_ENV
> \fBvault.env\fR in the config file > \fBtest\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-addr " URL"
Vault address.
.br
Precedence: this flag >
.B VAULT_ADDR
> \fBvault.addr\fR in the config file > \fBhttps://ssivault.fnal.gov:8200\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-path " PATH"
KV base path under which each secret section
.RI ( "e.g. tunnel" ,
see
.BR SECRET_REGISTRY " above) is stored. Normally computed from"
.B \-\-env
as
.IR okd/shared/<env>/mu2edaq-pager ;
setting this explicitly bypasses that computation entirely.
.br
Precedence: this flag >
.B VAULT_BASE_PATH
> \fBvault.base_path\fR in the config file > computed from
.BR \-\-env .
.TP
.BI \-\-kv\-mount " MOUNT"
KV v2 engine mount point.
.br
Precedence: this flag >
.B VAULT_KV_MOUNT
> \fBvault.kv_mount\fR in the config file > \fBokd\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
Vault token, overriding
.B VAULT_TOKEN
and
.IR ~/.vault-token .
Not recommended on a shared machine \(en prefer
.B vault login
so the token stays in your own home directory.
.TP
.B \-\-approle
Authenticate as the application rather than as a person: mint a short-lived
AppRole token by invoking
.BR get\-vault\-apptoken (1)
instead of reading
.IR ~/.vault\-token .
Intended for CI and unattended deploys. Off by default.
.br
Precedence: this flag >
.B MU2EDAQ_PAGER_VAULT_APPROLE
> \fBvault.approle\fR in the config file > off.
.br
An explicit
.B \-\-token
or
.B VAULT_TOKEN
disables AppRole minting, so a token already obtained by a calling script is
reused rather than a second one being created.
.TP
.BI \-\-approle\-role " NAME"
AppRole role name to use with
.BR \-\-approle .
.br
Precedence: this flag >
.B MU2EDAQ_PAGER_VAULT_ROLE
> \fBvault.role\fR in the config file.
.br
This role does not exist yet; when it does, it must carry a policy
granting read on
.IR okd/data/shared/{prod,test}/mu2edaq\-pager/* ;
see
.BR get\-vault\-apptoken (1).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Path to the YAML config file supplying connection defaults.
.br
Default:
.BR config/vault.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Secrets were fetched and rendered successfully.
.TP
.B 1
No Vault token was found, or the read failed (permissions, wrong path, or a
connection problem). A one-line, actionable message is printed to stderr \(en
never a raw stack trace.
.SH EXAMPLES
Print resolved test-instance secrets as shell-safe KEY=\(dqvalue\(dq lines:
.PP
.RS
.B python3 scripts/vault_client.py env \-\-env test
.RE
.PP
Render a production Helm values fragment and feed it straight into
.BR helm\ upgrade :
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 scripts/vault_client.py helm-values --env prod > /tmp/vault-values.yaml
helm upgrade --install mu2edaq-pager ./helm \e
    -f my-values.yaml -f /tmp/vault-values.yaml
.EE
.RE
.PP
Override the computed path entirely (e.g. a one-off dev path within the
same
.I okd
mount \(en note this is relative to the mount point, so it does NOT repeat
.IR okd/ ):
.PP
.RS
.B python3 scripts/vault_client.py env \-\-base\-path shared/dev/mu2edaq-pager
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B config/vault.yaml
Non-secret connection defaults (address, base path, KV mount). Committed to
git.
.TP
.B ~/.vault-token
Cached token written by
.BR "vault login" .
Read, never written, by this script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deploy\-okd\-proxy (1),
.BR get\-vault\-apptoken (1),
.B docs/Vault-Secrets.md ,
.B docs/okd-proxy-setup.md
.SH AUTHORS
mu2edaq-pager project contributors.
